<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n109825" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑφεῖσα</span></b> , 
			Ion.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὕπεισα</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>I placed under</i> or <i>secretly,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπείσας ἄνδρας</span> (
				Ion.
			
			part.) <i>having set</i> them <i>in ambush,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				3.126
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				6.103
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λόχον ὑφείσας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Nic.Dam.
					55J.
				</span></i>
			: but as (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑφ-</span>)<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἷσα</span> is the augmented aor. of <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἑδ-</span> (cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καθίζω,</span>
			
				Att.
			
			fut.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καθέσω</span>), the part.
			must be unaugmented, and <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπέσας,
			ὑπέσαντες</span> shd. be restored in <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
			</span></i> ll. cc., and either <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑφέσας</span>
			or the later form <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑφίσας [ῐ</span>] (cf.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑφίζω</span>) in Nic.Dam.l.c.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
